mutant: m062_stale_leader_fence_ignored
target: internal/catalog/scripts.go
failure-mode: |
  A catalog transaction whose fence bump loses to a newer epoch counts the
  failure but runs its body anyway (design D1). A deposed leader that is
  still running keeps writing hot batches, folds, and metadata next to its
  successor, so two writers interleave in the durable archive.
expected-detection: |
  The layer 3 oracle's stale_leader fault opens a session at the old epoch
  after a lease change and requires CommitMeta and CommitHotBatch to fail
  with ErrFenced and leave no key behind; every full seed fires it.
  TestScripts_FenceLost pins the same contract at the script layer.
expected-tier: disagg
tiers: disagg

